"To find the eighth term of the geometric sequence, we first need to determine the common ratio \\( r \\) and the first term \\( a \\).\n\nThe common ratio \\( r \\) is found by dividing the second term by the first term:\n\\[ r = \\frac{\\frac{25}{3}}{\\frac{125}{9}} = \\frac{25}{3} \\times \\frac{9}{125} = \\frac{3}{5} \\]\n\nThe first term \\( a \\) is given as \\( \\frac{125}{9} \\).\n\nThe eighth term \\( a_8 \\) of a geometric sequence is given by:\n\\[ a_8 = a \\cdot r^7 = \\frac{125}{9} \\cdot \\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^7 = \\frac{125}{9} \\cdot \\frac{2187}{3125} = \\frac{268775}{3125} \\]\n\nThus, the eighth term of the sequence is:\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{268775}{3125}} \\]"
"To solve the equation \\( |x-1| = 7 \\), we need to consider the definition of the absolute value function. The equation \\( |x-1| = 7 \\) means that the distance between \\( x \\) and 1 on the number line is 7. This can be expressed as two separate equations:\n\n1. \\( x - 1 = 7 \\)\n2. \\( x - 1 = -7 \\)\n\nLet's solve each equation separately:\n\n1. \\( x - 1 = 7 \\)\n   \\[\n   x = 7 + 1 = 8\n   \\]\n\n2. \\( x - 1 = -7 \\)\n   \\[\n   x = -7 + 1 = -6\n   \\]\n\nThe solutions to the equation \\( |x-1| = 7 \\) are \\( x = 8 \\) and \\( x = -6 \\). To find the sum of all values of \\( x \\), we add them together:\n\n\\[\n8 + (-6) = 8 - 6 = 2\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of all values of \\( x \\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\)."
