"To find the value of \\( c \\) given the function \\( f(x) = cx^3 - 9x + 3 \\) and the condition \\( f(2) = 9 \\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Substitute \\( x = 2 \\) into the function:\n   \\[\n   f(2) = c(2)^3 - 9(2) + 3\n   \\]\n\n2. Simplify the expression:\n   \\[\n   f(2) = c \\cdot 8 - 18 + 3\n   \\]\n  \\[\n   f(2) = 8c - 15\n   \\]\n\n3. Set the expression equal to 9 and solve for \\( c \\):\n   \\[\n   8c - 15 = 9\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   8c = 9 + 15\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   8c = 24\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   c = \\frac{24}{8}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( c \\) is \\(\\boxed{3}\\)."
