"To determine how many whole years it will take to recuperate the costs of the new green technology, we need to calculate the net annual savings and then determine how many years it will take for these savings to cover the one-time installation cost.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the net annual savings:\n- Annual energy savings: \\$1200\n- Annual maintenance costs: \\$650\n\nNet annual savings = Annual energy savings - Annual maintenance costs\nNet annual savings = \\$1200 - \\$650 = \\$550\n\nNext, we need to determine how many years it will take for the net annual savings to cover the one-time installation cost:\n- One-time installation cost: \\$10,000\n- Net annual savings: \\$550\n\nNumber of years = One-time installation cost / Net annual savings\nNumber of years = \\$10,000 / \\$550 ≈ 18.18\n\nSince we need a whole number of whole years, we round 18.18 to the next whole number, which is 19.\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is 19. I hope it is correct."
