"To determine the probability that Wilhelm marks the correct seats, we need to consider the total number of ways to choose 4 seats out of 6 and the number of ways to choose the 4 broken seats.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total number of ways to choose 4 seats out of 6. This is given by the combination formula:\n\\[\n\\binom{6}{4} = \\frac{6!}{4!(6-4)!} = \\frac{6!}{4!2!} = 15\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the number of ways to choose the 4 broken seats. Since there are 4 broken seats and we need to choose all 4 of them, there is only 1 way to do this.\n\nThe probability that Wilhelm marks the correct seats is the ratio of the number of favorable outcomes to the total number of outcomes:\n\\[\n\\text{Probability} = \\frac{\\text{Number of ways to choose 4 broken seats}}{\\text{Total number of ways to choose 4 seats}} = \\frac{1}{15}\n\\]\n\nThus, the probability that Wilhelm marks the correct seats is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{15}}\\)."
