"To determine how many positive integers are less than \\(100\\pi\\), we first need to approximate the value of \\(100\\pi\\).\n\nUsing the approximation \\(\\pi \\approx 3.14159\\), we calculate:\n\\[\n100\\pi \\approx 100 \\times 3.14159 = 314.159\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the largest integer less than 314.159. The largest integer less than 314.159 is 313.\n\nTherefore, the positive integers less than \\(100\\pi\\) are the integers from 1 to 313.\n\nTo find the number of these integers, we use the formula for the number of integers from \\(a\\) to \\(n\\), which is \\(n - a + 1\\).\n\nApplying this to the from 1 to 313:\n\\[\n313 - 1 + 1 = 313\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of positive integers less than \\(100\\pi\\) is \\(\\boxed{313}\\)."
