"To find the remainder when \\(301^4\\) is divided by 10,000, we can use modular arithmetic. First, we simplify \\(301 \\mod 10,000\\):\n\n\\[301 \\mod 10,000 = 301 - 10,000 = 301\\]\n\nNow, we need to find \\(301^4 \\mod 10,000\\). We can do this by squaring \\(301\\) multiple times and reducing modulo 10,000 at each step:\n\n\\[301^2 = 90601 \\mod 10,000 = 601\\]\n\\[301^4 = (301^2)^2 = 601^2 = 361201 \\mod 10,000 = 201\\]\n\nTherefore, the remainder when \\(301^4\\) is divided by 10,000 is \\(201\\).\n\nFinal Answer: \\boxed{201}"
