"To compute \\(\\dbinom{182}{180}\\), we can use the property of binomial coefficients that states:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{n}{k} = \\dbinom{n}{n - k}\n\\]\n\nIn this case, \\(n = 182\\) and \\(k = 180\\). Therefore, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{182}{180} = \\dbinom{182}{182 - 180} = \\dbinom{182}{2}\n\\]\n\nThe binomial coefficient \\(\\dbinom{182}{2}\\) is calculated as:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{182}{2} = \\frac{182!}{2! \\cdot 180!} = \\frac{182 \\times 181}{2 \\times 1} = \\frac{182 \\times 181}{2} = 16671\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{16671}\n\\]"
