"To compute \\(\\dbinom{85}{82}\\), we can use the property of binomial coefficients that states:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{n}{k} = \\dbinom{n}{n - k}\n\\]\n\nIn this case, \\(n = 85\\) and \\(k = 82\\). Therefore, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{85}{82} = \\dbinom{85}{85 - 82} = \\dbinom{85}{3}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to compute \\(\\dbinom{85}{3}\\). The binomial coefficient \\(\\dbinom{85}{3}\\) is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{85}{3} = \\frac{85!}{3! \\cdot 82!} = \\frac{85 \\cdot 84 \\cdot 83}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = \\frac{51840}{6} = 7140\n\\]\n\nFinal Answer:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{7140}\n\\]"
