"To find the greatest common factor (GCF) of \\(1001\\) and \\(2431\\), we can use the Euclidean algorithm. The Euclidean algorithm involves repeated division and taking remainders until we reach a remainder of \\(0\\).\n\n1. Divide \\(2431\\) by \\(1001\\) and find the remainder:\n   \\[\n   2431 \\div 1001 = 2 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 429\n   \\]\n\n2. Now, divide \\(1001\\) by the remainder \\(429\\) and find the new again:\n   \\[\n   1001 \\div 429 = 2 \\quad \\text{ remainder} \\quad 0\n   \\]\n\nSince the remainder is now \\(0\\), we stop here. The last non-zero remainder is \\(429\\).\n\nTherefore, the greatest common factor of \\(1001\\) and \\(2431\\) is \\( \\boxed{429}\\).\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\(429\\). I hope it is correct."
