"To determine how many feet Javier travels in one minute, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert Javier's speed from miles per hour to miles per minute.\n2. Convert the speed from miles per minute to feet per minute.\n\nFirst, let's convert Javier's speed from miles per hour to miles per minute. There are 60 minutes in an hour, so we divide the speed by 60:\n\n\\[ 15 \\text{ miles per hour} \\div 60 \\text{ minutes per hour} = 0.25 \\text{ miles per minute} \\]\n\nNext, we convert the speed from miles per minute to feet per minute. There are 5280 feet in a mile, so we multiply the speed by 5280:\n\n\\[ 0.25 \\text{ miles per minute} \\times 5280 \\text{ feet per mile} = 1320 \\text{ feet per minute} \\]\n\nTherefore, Javier travels \\boxed{1320} feet in one minute.\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $1320$. I hope it is correct."
"To solve the equation \\(3a - 7(3 - a) = 5\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Distribute the \\(-7\\) through the parentheses:\n   \\[\n   3a - 21 + 7a = 5\n   \\]\n\n2. Combine like terms:\n   \\[\n   10a - 21 = 5\n   \\]\n\n3. Add 21 to both sides to isolate the term with \\(a\\):\n   \\[\n   10a - 21 + 21 = 5 + 21\n   \\]\n\n4. Simplify both sides:\n   \\[\n   10a = 26\n   \\]\n\n5. Divide both sides by 10 to solve for \\(a\\):\n   \\[\n   a = \\frac{26}{10}\n   \\]\n\n6. Simplify the fraction:\n   \\[\n   a = \\frac{13}{5}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the solution is:\n\\[\n\\(\\boxed{\\frac{13}{5}}\\)"
