"To find the greatest prime factor of 3105, we first need to determine its prime factorization.\n\n1. Divide 3105 by the smallest prime number, which is 3:\n   \\[\n   3105 \\div 3 = 1035\n   \\]\n\n2. Divide 1035 by the next smallest prime number, which is 5:\n   \\[\n   1035 \\div 5 = 207\n   \\]\n\n3. Divide 207 by the next smallest prime number, which is 9:\n   \\[\n   207 \\div 9 = 23\n   \\]\n\n4. 23 is a prime number.\n\nSo, the prime factorization of 3105 is:\n\\[\n3105 = 3 \\times 5 \\times 9 \\times 23\n\\]\n\nThe prime factors of 3105 are 3, 5, 9, and 23.\n\nTherefore, the greatest prime factor of 3105 is \\(\\boxed{23}\\)."
