"Let \\( d \\) be the number of dresses produced and \\( s \\) be the number of shirts produced. According to the problem, the factory produces 3 dresses for every 5 shirts. This can be expressed as:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{d}{s} = \\frac{3}{5}\n\\]\n\nWe also know that the total number of garments produced is 72:\n\n\\[\nd + s = 72\n\\]\n\nWe can solve these two equations simultaneously. First, express \\( d \\) in terms of \\( s \\):\n\n\\[\nd = \\frac{3}{5}s\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\( d \\) in the second equation:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3}{5}s + s = 72\n\\]\n\nCombine the terms:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{8}{5}s = 72\n\\]\n\nSolve for \\( s \\):\n\n\\[\ns = 45\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute back for \\( d \\):\n\n\\[\nd = \\frac{3}{5} \\times 45 = 27\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of dresses produced is \\(\\boxed{27}\\)."
