"To find the measure of an interior angle of a regular octagon, we can use the formula for the sum of the interior angles of a polygon:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Sum of interior angles} = (n-2) \\times 180^\\circ\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( n \\) is the number of sides of the polygon. For an octagon, \\( n = 8 \\).\n\nFirst, calculate the sum of the interior angles:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Sum of interior angles} = (8-2) \\times 180^\\circ = 6 \\times 180^\\circ = 1080^\\circ\n\\]\n\nSince the octagon is regular, all its interior angles are equal. Therefore, the measure of each interior angle is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Measure of each interior angle} = \\frac{\\text{Sum of interior angles}}{n} = \\frac{1080^\\circ}{8} = 135^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus, the measure of an interior angle of the regular octagon is \\(\\boxed{135^\\circ}\\).\n\nThe final answer is \\(135\\) degrees."
