"To compute \\(\\tan 15^\\circ\\), we can use the tangent addition formula for two angles, which states:\n\n\\[\n\\tan(a + b) = \\frac{\\tan a + \\tan b}{1 - \\tan a \\tan b}\n\\]\n\nWe can express \\(15^\\circ\\) as \\(45^\\circ + 0^\\circ\\). Therefore, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\tan 15^\\circ = \\tan(45^\\circ + 0^\\circ) = \\frac{\\tan 45^\\circ + \\tan 0^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 45^\\circ \\tan 0^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nWe know that \\(\\tan 45^\\circ = 1\\) and \\(\\tan 0^\\circ = 0\\). Substituting these values into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\tan 15^\\circ = \\frac{1 + 0}{1 - 1 \\cdot 0} = \\frac{1}{1 - 0} = 1\n\\]\n\nThus, the final value of \\(\\tan 15^\\circ\\) is \\(\\boxed{1}\\)."
